ces":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11817},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62319131,"created":"2026-10-16T04:12:09.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":2,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11184,"number":2,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 4:12 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:11","question":{"id":164472,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":12559,"text":"<p>Identify the following surface: \n\\[\nz = \\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{25} - \\dfrac{(y+1)^2}{16}\n\\]</p>\n","choice1":"A hyperbolic paraboloid","choice2":"An elliptic paraboloid","choice3":"An elliptic cylinder","choice4":"A hyperbolic cylinder","choice5":"An elliptic cone","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>Recall that the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $O$ is given by</p>\n<p>\\[\nz = \\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}-\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2},\n\\]</p>\n<p>and a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ is given by</p>\n<p>\\[\nz - z_0 = \\dfrac{(x-x_0)^2}{a^2}-\\dfrac{(y-y_0)^2}{b^2},\n\\]</p>\n<p>Thus, our equation is a hyperbolic paraboloid with the following parameters:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(x_0,y_0,z_0) = (1,-1,0), \\quad a=5, \\quad b=4.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":1898,"name":"Identifying Quadric Surfaces"},"example":{"id":12559,"title":"Identifying Quadric Surfaces and Cylinders"},"group":{"id":12592,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14253581,"answer":{"id":62319131,"cread":"2026-10-16T04:12:09.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":2,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11184},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62319138,"created":"2026-10-16T04:12:25.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13986,"number":3,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 4:12 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":164475,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":12559,"text":"<p>Identify the surface $\\dfrac{z^2}9 = 9x^2+\\dfrac{y^2}{81}.$</p>\n","choice1":"An elliptic cone","choice2":"A hyperboloid of one sheet","choice3":"A hyperboloid of two sheets","choice4":"An ellipsoid","choice5":"An elliptic paraboloid","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>Recall that the equation of an elliptic cone centered at $O$ is given by</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\dfrac{z^2}{c^2} = \\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Thus, our equation is an elliptic cone with $a= \\dfrac13, \\quad b =9, \\quad c=3.$</p>\n","topic":{"id":1898,"name":"Identifying Quadric Surfaces"},"example":{"id":12559,"title":"Identifying Quadric Surfaces and Cylinders"},"group":{"id":12592,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14253581,"answer":{"id":62319138,"cread":"2026-10-16T04:12:25.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13986},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62319154,"created":"2026-10-16T04:12:42.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":3,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12569,"number":4,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 4:12 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":164481,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":12559,"text":"<p>Identify the following surface: \n\\[\n(x+2)^2 -(y-1)^2 = 1, \\quad -\\infty &lt; z &lt; \\infty\n\\]</p>\n","choice1":"A hyperbolic cylinder","choice2":"An elliptic cylinder","choice3":"A hyperbolic paraboloid","choice4":"An elliptic cone","choice5":"A hyperboloid","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>Recall that the equation of a hyperbolic cylinder, whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis, is given by</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}-\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2} = 1,\n\\]</p>\n<p>and a hyperbolic cylinder, whose axis of symmetry is parallel to the $z$-axis and passes through the point $(x_0, y_0)$ in the $xy$-plane, is given by</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\dfrac{(x-x_0)^2}{a^2}-\\dfrac{(y-y_0)^2}{b^2} = 1.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Thus, our equation is a hyperbolic cylinder with the following parameters:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(x_0,y_0) = (-2,1), \\quad a= b=1.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":1898,"name":"Identifying Quadric Surfaces"},"example":{"id":12559,"title":"Identifying Quadric Surfaces and Cylinders"},"group":{"id":12592,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14253581,"answer":{"id":62319154,"cread":"2026-10-16T04:12:42.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":3,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12569},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62319167,"created":"2026-10-16T04:12:59.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12408,"number":5,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 4:12 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":164516,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":12560,"text":"<p>Identify the following surface: </p>\n<p>\\[y^2+z^2=1, \\quad -\\infty &lt; x &lt; \\infty.\\]</p>\n","choice1":"An elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis","choice2":"An elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis","choice3":"A hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis","choice4":"A hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis","choice5":"A hyperbolic paraboloid whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>Recall that the equation of an elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Thus, an elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $\\boldsymbol x$<strong>-axis</strong> is given by</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}+\\dfrac{z^2}{c^2}=1.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Therefore, our equation is an elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis and $b=c=1.$</p>\n","topi